[{"sha":"70dc164847bb029321a3d0eea9b74db1fdb48055","node_id":"C_kwDOAQzde9oAKDcwZGMxNjQ4NDdiYjAyOTMyMWEzZDBlZWE5Yjc0ZGIxZmRiNDgwNTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"David Fowler","email":"davidfowl@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-05T18:24:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-05T18:24:50Z"},"message":"Reduce allocations in managed DataProtection protect/unprotect (#70146)\n\n* Reduce allocations in managed DataProtection protect/unprotect\n\n- ManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor: use a single SymmetricAlgorithm instance for\n  sizing and encryption (previously up to 3 per Protect, one never disposed),\n  and implement IOptimizedAuthenticatedEncryptor so the payload is encrypted\n  directly into the final array including the key ring header pre-buffer.\n- ManagedSP800_108_CTR_HMACSHA512: raise PRF input stackalloc threshold from\n  128 to 512 bytes. AAD (app discriminator + purposes) routinely pushes the\n  input above 128 bytes, causing a heap allocation per Protect/Unprotect.\n- Add KeyRingProtectorBenchmarks and tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Avoid unsafe APIs and larger stackalloc in DataProtection perf change\n\n- Replace Unsafe.AreSame/MemoryMarshal assert with a safe Span.Overlaps check\n  and drop the now-unused usings.\n- Keep the SP800-108 PRF input stackalloc at 128 bytes; rent from ArrayPool\n  (cleared on return) above that instead of heap-allocating.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Write SP800-108 separator byte explicitly now that the PRF input may be rented\n\nThe 0x00 separator between label and context was never written and relied on a\nzero-initialized buffer. Pooled arrays are not zeroed, which produced wrong\nsubkeys (seen as cookie auth failures in AuthSamples.FunctionalTests). Write it\nexplicitly and make the reference test leave dirty data in the pool first.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Pin managed encryptor and isolated key ring in KeyRingProtectorBenchmarks\n\nOn Windows the default AES-256-CBC/HMACSHA256 key maps to the CNG encryptor,\nand the benchmark reused the user-profile key ring. Use\nManagedAuthenticatedEncryptorConfiguration with a temp key directory so\nManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor is measured on every OS.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Retrigger CI\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use new byte[] instead of ArrayPool for KDF input; add managed encryptor round-trip tests\n\nThe PRF input contains key derivation material, so don't place it in shared pooled\nmemory. Raise the constant stack buffer to 256 bytes to cover longer AAD (purpose)\nvalues and fall back to a new array above that.\n\nAdd tests that go through AuthenticatedEncryptorExtensions.Encrypt (IOptimizedAuthenticatedEncryptor)\nand KeyRingBasedDataProtector.Protect/Unprotect with a real managed CBC encryptor, with\ncases on both sides of the 128- and 256-byte KDF input thresholds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address review feedback: inline stack buffer size, simplify comments\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: davidfowl <95136+davidfowl@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cfc1cc88bfee9c5a2b8834995a872cfdc4b812ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/git/trees/cfc1cc88bfee9c5a2b8834995a872cfdc4b812ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/git/commits/70dc164847bb029321a3d0eea9b74db1fdb48055","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq7MnyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6AkQAIEHmBbrsRWw4gP7SC2ml3Ys\noqlXcvKacJL1BvH3dCj3esB8cphR8DUMgmr5caOFHDKzSVDL41iJRxes86enLSA3\n6wSrFre3haXliqo/7GPrBKsiKhrYIiWad6bMnIOtl1xmbs6RhPhbkPSorxt7Aeib\nuzihDSM8H4YxbWfpy5n0u30REufYYPVqjnDxJyVHmyj+D0E/E3MHCli2e9JQHBXN\nTL1g+ymOvZnuo4QDpN3+XxiW/BOL5QnSFC2BgONSdL/tuwIgO43swvM+fWc5ftn8\ntvhJoqIjI8RwTtMnPnZPrPNkmZEf2xCNeUHunT9pHtNZ3/yh/EBIZMI2wNqmmw0W\nJEFLeIGBYvBV7otKUdJxY2MfmQ2B+80pWoZLUfKbwhr7JBq0DcHASoa0bkYJJNml\nxe+Lr7qLSIc1HwPPNWqUMb83CW/6tv5xZw6k7Xa7vm0pclNpDewHnqiB6VFgBZL/\n7rKPspBLYyNWenn0FD9QAmNqWOCyOuS/EEs2yW7EChyVgAlgzqNxyjl88kdK2UdN\nXUbo3U04B9Sb7altY7y3W2M30Yl0VAOWEwD/rnwBpmSYbnJKxxexKWs5Pg2lScnf\na5dfyyvEGCfT4vCC3IxNibs4eauWuFH12sEClmJjLs7MNHsoPcAeNCXTmLFtgWf5\npmlDpxTSyd8FAal+mPW1\n=xxAE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cfc1cc88bfee9c5a2b8834995a872cfdc4b812ad\nparent c342e77482bd7837a2e00b1e75546b795aa8c51d\nauthor David Fowler <davidfowl@gmail.com> 1793903090 -0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793903090 +0000\n\nReduce allocations in managed DataProtection protect/unprotect (#70146)\n\n* Reduce allocations in managed DataProtection protect/unprotect\n\n- ManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor: use a single SymmetricAlgorithm instance for\n  sizing and encryption (previously up to 3 per Protect, one never disposed),\n  and implement IOptimizedAuthenticatedEncryptor so the payload is encrypted\n  directly into the final array including the key ring header pre-buffer.\n- ManagedSP800_108_CTR_HMACSHA512: raise PRF input stackalloc threshold from\n  128 to 512 bytes. AAD (app discriminator + purposes) routinely pushes the\n  input above 128 bytes, causing a heap allocation per Protect/Unprotect.\n- Add KeyRingProtectorBenchmarks and tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Avoid unsafe APIs and larger stackalloc in DataProtection perf change\n\n- Replace Unsafe.AreSame/MemoryMarshal assert with a safe Span.Overlaps check\n  and drop the now-unused usings.\n- Keep the SP800-108 PRF input stackalloc at 128 bytes; rent from ArrayPool\n  (cleared on return) above that instead of heap-allocating.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Write SP800-108 separator byte explicitly now that the PRF input may be rented\n\nThe 0x00 separator between label and context was never written and relied on a\nzero-initialized buffer. Pooled arrays are not zeroed, which produced wrong\nsubkeys (seen as cookie auth failures in AuthSamples.FunctionalTests). Write it\nexplicitly and make the reference test leave dirty data in the pool first.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Pin managed encryptor and isolated key ring in KeyRingProtectorBenchmarks\n\nOn Windows the default AES-256-CBC/HMACSHA256 key maps to the CNG encryptor,\nand the benchmark reused the user-profile key ring. Use\nManagedAuthenticatedEncryptorConfiguration with a temp key directory so\nManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor is measured on every OS.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Retrigger CI\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use new byte[] instead of ArrayPool for KDF input; add managed encryptor round-trip tests\n\nThe PRF input contains key derivation material, so don't place it in shared pooled\nmemory. Raise the constant stack buffer to 256 bytes to cover longer AAD (purpose)\nvalues and fall back to a new array above that.\n\nAdd tests that go through AuthenticatedEncryptorExtensions.Encrypt (IOptimizedAuthenticatedEncryptor)\nand KeyRingBasedDataProtector.Protect/Unprotect with a real managed CBC encryptor, with\ncases on both sides of the 128- and 256-byte KDF input thresholds.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address review feedback: inline stack buffer size, simplify comments\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: davidfowl <95136+davidfowl@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-11-05T18:24:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/commits/70dc164847bb029321a3d0eea9b74db1fdb48055","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/commit/70dc164847bb029321a3d0eea9b74db1fdb48055","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/commits/70dc164847bb029321a3d0eea9b74db1fdb48055/comments","author":{"login":"davidfowl","id":95136,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1MTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95136?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfowl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https: